> let f of x be x squared plus 1 where x is between 0 and 10
  ucas: f(x in 0..10) = x^2 + 1
  ucas: show f
f(x: int in 0..10) = x^2 + 1
  -> int
> what is its range?
  ucas: range f
range of f -> int:
  1..101
  fits in u7
  over all 11 points of the domain
> what is f when x is 3?
  ucas: f(3)
10
> what is f of 2?
  ucas: f(2)
5
> f of 5
  ucas: f(5)
26
> let g of x be 2 x plus 1
  ucas: g(x) = 2*x + 1
  ucas: show g
g(x: real) = 2x + 1
  -> real
> call it twice_one
  ucas: twice_one(x: real) = g(x)
  ucas: show twice_one
twice_one(x: real) = 2x + 1
  -> real
> what is twice_one of 4?
  ucas: twice_one(4)
9
> what is g of 4?
  ucas: g(4)
9
> let h of p and q be p times q plus 1
  ucas: h(p, q) = p*q + 1
  ucas: show h
h(p: real, q: real) = p*q + 1
  -> real
> what is h of 2 and 3?
  ucas: h(2, 3)
7
> define k of x as x cubed
  ucas: k(x) = x^3
  ucas: show k
k(x: real) = x^3
  -> real
> what is k of 3?
  ucas: k(3)
27
> f(x) = x^2 + 2x + 1
> what is the range of f for x from 0 to 3?
  ucas: it(x: real in 0..3) = f(x)
  ucas: range it
range of it:
  [1, 16]   min at x ≈ 0, max at x ≈ 3
  grid of 20001 points over [0, 3], extrema refined at critical points
> what are the roots of f?
  ucas: zeros f
zeros of f:
  1 zero:
    x = -1 (multiplicity 2)
  proved: a polynomial of degree 2 has 2 roots counted with multiplicity
> g of x is 3x minus 1
  ucas: g(x) = 3*x - 1
  ucas: show g
g(x: real) = 3x - 1
  -> real
> what is g of 2?
  ucas: g(2)
5
> let p of x be x cubed minus 3x
  ucas: p(x) = x^3 - 3*x
  ucas: show p
p(x: real) = x^3 - 3x
  -> real
> what are the critical points of p?
  ucas: crit p
critical points of p:
  p' = 3x^2 - 3
  x ≈ -1: local maximum, p = 2
  x ≈ 1: local minimum, p = -2
  searched [-10, 10] (default; give x a range)
> what is the derivative of p?
  ucas: diff p
d/dx p = 3x^2 - 3
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> what is the second derivative of p?
  ucas: diff p 2
d/dx p = 3x^2 - 3
d²/dx² p = 6x
  holds for every real x
  check: each order matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> let y be 5
  ucas: y = 5
  ucas: show y
y() = 5
  -> int
> what is y plus 1?
  ucas: y + 1
6
> x if x is positive, otherwise minus x; call it myabs
  ucas: it(x) = x > 0 ? x : -x
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = x > 0 ? x : -x
  -> real
  ucas: myabs(x: real) = it(x)
  ucas: show myabs
myabs(x: real) = x > 0 ? x : -x
  -> real
> what is the derivative of myabs?
  ucas: diff myabs
d/dx myabs = x > 0 ? 1 : -1
  holds for x != 0
    at x = 0 myabs has a corner (slope -1 from the left, 1 from the right)
    (points looked for in [-10, 10])
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 1e-15)
> what is myabs of -3?
  ucas: myabs(-3)
3
> what is the range of myabs for x from -4 to 4?
  ucas: it(x: real in -4..4) = myabs(x)
  ucas: range it
range of it:
  [-0, 4]   min at x ≈ 0, max at x ≈ -4
  grid of 20001 points over [-4, 4], extrema refined at critical points
> x is a byte
  note: "byte" without signed or unsigned: read as unsigned, u8, not signed, i8 (say "unsigned byte", or "assume bytes are signed")
  ok: from now on x is a byte
> what is the range of x plus 1?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x + 1
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u8:
  0..255   (256 distinct values)
  fits in u8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> assume q is a signed byte
  ok: from now on q is a signed byte
> what is the range of q?
  ucas: it(q: i8) = q
  ucas: range it
range of it -> i8:
  -128..127   (256 distinct values)
  fits in i8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> what is the range of x plus 1 for an unsigned byte x?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x + 1
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u8:
  0..255   (256 distinct values)
  fits in u8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> what is the range of n for an integer n between 1 and 12?
  note: "integer" without a width: read as an unbounded integer, int, not a C int, i32 (say "32-bit integer", or "assume integers are 32-bit")
  ucas: it(n: int in 1..12) = n
  ucas: range it
range of it -> int:
  1..12
  fits in u4
  over all 12 points of the domain
> what is the range of 2 to the n for n between 0 and 10?
  ucas: it(n in 0..10) = 2^n
  ucas: range it
range of it -> int:
  1..1024
  fits in u11
  over all 11 points of the domain
> does x times x overflow for a 16-bit unsigned x?
  ucas: it(x: u16) = x*x
  ucas: wrap it
wrap analysis of it:
  x*x   (u16)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 65280 points, e.g. x=256
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 65173 points, e.g. x=182
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 65280 points, e.g. x=256
      exact for: 0..255
  over all 65536 points of the domain
> what is the range of x divided by 2 for a 32-bit signed x?
  ucas: it(x: i32) = x/2
  ucas: range it
range of it -> i32:
  -1073741824..1073741823  (sampled min/max; not a sound bound)
  fits in i31
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4294967296 points); not exhaustive
  sound bound (intervals): -2147483648..2147483647
> avg(a: u8, b: u8) = (a + b) / 2
> does avg overflow?
  ucas: wrap avg
wrap analysis of avg:
  a + b   (u8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 32640 points, e.g. a=255, b=1
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 16384 points, e.g. a=127, b=1
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 32640 points, e.g. a=255, b=1
  over all 65536 points of the domain
> is avg equal to (a & b) + ((a xor b) >> 1)?
  ucas: that(a: u8, b: u8) = (a & b) + ((a xor b) >> 1)
  ucas: equiv avg that
avg and that differ at 32640 points, e.g. a=255, b=1: 0 vs 128
> is avg commutative?
  note: commutative: avg(a, b) = avg(b, a) everywhere?
  ucas: lhs(a: u8, b: u8) = avg(a, b)
  ucas: rhs(a: u8, b: u8) = avg(b, a)
  ucas: equiv lhs rhs
lhs and rhs are equal on the domain of lhs (exhaustive)
